    "description": "Landmark Dividend acquires, develops, and manages real-estate interests and infrastructure tied to wireless communications, data centers, outdoor advertising, and renewable-power sites. Its customer base includes tower operators, data-center users, enterprise customers, municipalities, faith-based organizations, and other landowners and infrastructure counterparties. The company follows an asset-heavy model focused on long-duration ground leases, digital real estate interests, and related infrastructure ownership structures. Public materials describe a portfolio of more than 5,000 assets and a business model centered on acquiring and managing mission-critical site interests. The platform has been part of DigitalBridge's digital infrastructure ecosystem and remains active across wireless, data-center, and adjacent infrastructure verticals. ADIA completed the acquisition of a 40% stake in Landmark in April 2024 alongside DigitalBridge-sponsored vehicles, with DigitalBridge retaining the balance.",
